{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChK4faxhwPAfB4qVruhVX","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"`FilePathField` now accepts a callable for `path`, so the migration records the callable instead of the machine-specific resolved path. I haven't run any tests or tried it with a callable.\n\nThe change is one line in `FilePathField.formfield()` in `django/db/models/fields/__init__.py`. It calls `path` if it's callable and passes the result to the form field. `deconstruct()` already writes `self.path` as-is, so `makemigrations` should now write the callable itself.\n\nTwo gaps remain. I didn't add a check or docs for the callable case. Anything that reads `field.path` on the model field directly, rather than through `formfield()`, still gets the callable."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":657,"cache_read_input_tokens":19824,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":657},"output_tokens":216,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c9f535a4-fc4d-4edc-8e59-5d215c91e9e1","uuid":"03591543-44a3-426d-b103-c69fa6763359","timestamp":"2026-11-23T02:23:08.077Z","request_id":"req_011ChK4fapmpXJjsQPQPD9Ms"}
